{"slug":"security-camera-placement",
 "title":"Where to Mount a Security Camera (Installer Tips) #shorts",
 "beats":[
  {"text":"Most people mount their security camera in the wrong spot. Here's where I put them."},
  {"text":"First, go high, but not too high. Around eight to ten feet keeps it out of reach and still sees faces."},
  {"text":"Second, cover the entry points. Front door, back door, and the driveway. That's where people actually come in."},
  {"text":"Third, watch the sun. A camera facing east or west can get blinded at sunrise or sunset."},
  {"text":"Fourth, check the Wi-Fi right where it mounts, before you drill."},
  {"text":"And respect privacy. Don't point it into your neighbor's windows."},
  {"text":"High, on the doors, out of the sun, strong Wi-Fi. Follow NovaProHome for more install tips."}
 ],
